G4 → G4.1, G4.2, G4.3 | OR | Multiple dish retrieval methods exist; the system falls back through alternatives if one method is unavailable.  
G5 → G5.1, G5.2 | OR | Door opening can be performed either by robot cooperation or by human assistance.  
G2.2 → G2.2.1 and AT2 | AND | Tray delivery requires first querying availability (G2.2.1) and then executing the tray delivery (AT2).  
G3 → AT3 and AT4 | AND | Meal tracking involves updating the log and alerting if the wrong meal is retrieved.  
G6 → AT5 and AT6 | AND | Meal identification requires both announcement and confirmation to ensure the correct meal is selected.  
G1 → G2, G3, G4, G5, G6 | AND | The top-level goal requires all sub-goals (food delivery, tracking, dish retrieval, door opening, and meal identification) to be completed for mission success.

Task Relationships:  
• G2.1 → AT1 | AND | Navigation is required for direct table delivery.  
• G2.2 → AT2 | AND | Tray delivery execution follows the availability query.  
• G4.1 → AT7 | AND | Dish pickup by a single robot.  
• G4.2 → AT8 | AND | Coordination with a second robot for dish pickup.  
• G4.3 → AT9 | AND | Coordination with human assistance for dish pickup.  
• G5.1 → AT10 | AND | Door opening via robot cooperation.  
• G5.2 → AT11 | AND | Door opening via human assistance.

